{
  "schema_version": "1.7.0",
  "id": "USN-8977-1",
  "summary": "bitlbee vulnerabilities",
  "details": "It was discovered that BitlBee incorrectly handled file transfer\nconnections that expired when built with libpurple. A remote attacker could\npossibly use this issue to cause BitlBee to crash, resulting in a denial of\nservice, or possibly execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2016-10188)\n\nIt was discovered that BitlBee incorrectly handled file transfer requests\nfor contacts that were not in the contact list. A remote attacker could\npossibly use this issue to cause BitlBee to crash, resulting in a denial of\nservice, or possibly execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2016-10189)",
